    "exitSkills": [
      "Can identify initial /m/, /s/ and /t/ and match M/m, S/s and T/t to their sounds.",
      "Can identify short /a/ as the middle sound in familiar CVC words and is ready for oral blending.",
      "Can orally blend familiar /m/, /s/, /t/ and /a/ phonemes into simple CVC words.",
      "Can decode familiar printed CVC words containing m, s, t and short a from left to right.",
      "Can segment familiar CVC words into ordered phonemes and is ready for sound-to-letter spelling.",
      "Can segment familiar CVC words and map their phonemes to m, s, t and short-a graphemes for spelling.",
      "Can read familiar CVC words accurately and reread them with early automaticity.",
      "Can recognise taught CVC word-family patterns and use them as support while decoding every grapheme.",
      "Can decode short controlled CVC sentences and answer literal meaning questions.",
      "Can read a short controlled passage, retain key details and answer text-based sequencing questions.",
      "Can demonstrate the taught foundational skills and identify a specific area for targeted remediation.",
      "Can use diagnostic evidence to select targeted practice and verify improvement through reassessment."
